      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Waluipedia cast sheet — King Boo.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-character-sheets.py</code>, hand-authored from the article. XP ledger: level 2, power rating 12 → a level 2 Warlock player-character sheet (a player may take this seat; the authored CR 2 stands in where the ledger is silent). Numbers are a GM-ready reading of the record, not a filed stat line; the article stays the authority. Archive date 1040 BF.</p><p><strong>The Crown That Watches From The Wrong Side of Every Mirror</strong> — Unknown — operates independently of every known faction, which is itself alarming</p><p>Status: Active — precise location unknown; influence confirmed across multiple planes</p><p>King Boo is the sovereign of the Boo collective and one of the few entities in the current crisis that Waluigi cannot adequately categorize. Most threats in this investigation are comprehensible: the Iron Legion wants control, the Loyalists want justice, the Corvinarus family wants succession, Wario wants money. King Boo wants something that Waluigi has not yet been able to name. He has been present—obliquely, through his subjects and through mirror-adjacent phenomena—in more moments of the Raventree crisis than coincidence can explain. His Boos haunt the manor's mirror layer. His subjects provide intelligence that is accurate often enough to be credible and fabricated often enough to be dangerous. He is connected to Luigi through Luigi's ghost-hunting career in ways that have never been fully explained. And he exists in a dimension where observation is itself participation—where watching something is a form of touching it. Waluigi does not like being watched. Waluigi especially does not like being watched by something that thinks watching IS doing. WAH.</p><h3>Evidence</h3><ul><li><strong>Crown's Chill</strong> — “The Crown That Watches From The Wrong Side of Every Mirror”</li><li><strong>Incorporeal Movement</strong> — “The Crown That Watches From The Wrong Side of Every Mirror”</li><li><strong>Sovereign of the Boo Collective</strong> — “The crown—which King Boo wears with the confidence of someone who did not find it lying around but MANIFESTED it—represents sovereign authority over the Boo collective.”</li><li><strong>Watcher Across Planes</strong> — “Active — precise location unknown; influence confirmed across multiple planes”</li><li><strong>Terrifying Visage</strong> — “He is connected to Luigi through Luigi's ghost-hunting career in ways that have never been fully explained.”</li></ul><p>Article: <code>#/article/king_boo</code> (characters). Site sheet: <code>#/sheets/king_boo</code>.</p>",
        "public": ""
      }
    },
